WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:19.596
The OWASP Top 10 provides a practical recap of application risks: broken access control, cryptographic failures, injection, insecure design, misconfiguration, vulnerable components, authentication failures, integrity failures, logging failures, and SSRF.

2
00:00:19.596 --> 00:00:33.474
SOC 2 Trust Services Criteria help translate those risks into control expectations around logical access, system operations, monitoring, risk mitigation, change management, and data protection.

3
00:00:33.474 --> 00:00:39.102
Application security in cloud and SaaS environments is inseparable from customer trust.

4
00:00:39.102 --> 00:00:46.735
Customers expect secure design, reliable access controls, monitored operations, and disciplined change management.

5
00:00:46.735 --> 00:00:49.599
Completion of this course is awareness-level only.

6
00:00:49.599 --> 00:00:56.583
It does not constitute SOC 2 certification, audit completion, or proof of full organizational compliance.

7
00:00:56.583 --> 00:01:12.587
Useful follow-on materials include OWASP references, SOC 2 TSC references, secure coding checklists, a glossary, an OWASP-to-SOC 2 mapping matrix, developer quick-reference guides, and SaaS security checklists.

8
00:01:12.587 --> 00:01:15.152
Use this course as an awareness and planning aid.

9
00:01:15.152 --> 00:01:19.831
Validate criteria applicability with audit and compliance stakeholders.

10
00:01:19.831 --> 00:01:27.165
Maintain evidence for secure development, monitoring, access control, change management, and remediation activities.

11
00:01:27.165 --> 00:01:31.286
Selected SOC 2 mappings for this topic include CC6.

12
00:01:31.286 --> 00:01:34.559
1 - Logical access controls; CC7.

13
00:01:34.559 --> 00:01:37.422
1 - Vulnerability management; CC8.

14
00:01:37.422 --> 00:01:39.458
1 - Change management processes.
